WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.490
- Alright, y'all know I
always like to close an hour

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.280
with something I hope will
bring extra joy in your day.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.499
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:09.750
(jazz music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.300
Sadly, the war in
Ukraine is still going on

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.310
and it's absolutely
devastating and heartbreaking

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.590
but one New Yorker is
giving Ukrainian kids

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.920
the chance to just be kids
through the magic of baseball.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.200
Jordan Baltimore runs
a baseball program here

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.900
in the city, and he's also
created a not-for-profit

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.850
that makes the sport accessible

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.040
in the most underserved parts of New York.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.750
Recently, he took a few of his players

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.540
to Poland to teach
displaced Ukrainian orphans

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.280
the beloved all American sport

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.700
and the impacts have proven to
be long lasting for everyone.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.519
We have Jordan with us now.

00:00:40.519 --> 00:00:41.633
(crowd cheering and clapping)
Hi Jordan.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.660
So tell us about this trip to Poland.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.790
- So when the war began, uh,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.590
we immediately mobilized the nonprofit

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.960
and began raising money for and donating

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.830
to organizations on the
ground in Warsaw, in Ukraine.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.230
And I felt like we needed to do more.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.160
I knew we needed to do more.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.680
And one of the moms in
our program introduced us

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.990
to the SOK foundation over in Warsaw

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.260
and they're doing an incredible
job of feeding and caring

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.560
for orphans who have
come over from Ukraine.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.400
Um 650 of them are now in one orphanage

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.140
on the outskirts of Warsaw.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.730
And that conversation
with SOK foundation led

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.421
to a trip, four days six children

00:01:23.421 --> 00:01:26.160
that came with me and
their families joined us.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.060
- Wow.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:27.893
- We went there,

00:01:27.893 --> 00:01:30.060
we thought we were going
to be teaching baseball.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.820
We ended up cooking,
cleaning, serving food

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.870
to thousands of refugees
in and around Warsaw.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.390
And then we spent two
days teaching baseball too

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.290
and playing baseball

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.750
with hundreds of
Ukrainian orphan refugees.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.510
And if you want to put
things in perspective,

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:48.180
walk into an orphanage
where you see 650 children

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.530
with no parents.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.240
And it meant so much to us.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.840
It was emotionally overwhelming.

00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:56.100
Uh, the next day we were on
the baseball field with them

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.780
teaching how to run the bases.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.613
- Yeah.

00:01:58.613 --> 00:01:59.446
- Throwing catch,
- Yeah.

00:01:59.446 --> 00:02:00.840
- Hit a baseball, and it all culminated

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.608
in the American school of
Warsaw with a baseball game.

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:05.160
- That's amazing.
- And-

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.520
Well, since then, we've raised
$50,000 and we've donated

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.030
to the SOK foundation there
and we're now back in touch

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.130
with the children and planning what's next

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:15.210
and when we're going back.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.470
- It's so cool what you're doing,

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.422
I'm liking your post right now, Jordan.

00:02:18.422 --> 00:02:19.440
(doorbell ringing)
(audience clapping)

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.700
- And that's not all.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.250
Our season long partner,
Pilot, pen makers of G2,

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.140
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.830
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, sir.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.620
And so they're gonna be writing
a check to Sharing Empire

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.617
for a thousand dollars just to help out.

00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:34.450
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.320
Thank you for what you're
doing, it's so cool.

00:02:37.173 --> 00:02:38.006
So very cool.

00:02:38.006 --> 00:02:38.904
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:38.904 --> 00:02:39.737
That's not all.

00:02:39.737 --> 00:02:40.810
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.290
Pilot, America's number one pen

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.490
is partnering with
America's number one team

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.390
and they're giving
everyone in the audience

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.520
and all of our guests four tickets

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.893
to a 2022 New York Yankees
regular season game.

00:02:53.893 --> 00:02:55.897
(audience cheering and clapping)

